  "title": "Entente Cordiale",
  "summary": "On 8 April 1904 Britain and France signed agreements in London settling a number of colonial disputes. The package included a declaration on Egypt and Morocco, a convention on Newfoundland and West and Central Africa, and a declaration on Siam, Madagascar and the New Hebrides. It was an understanding, not a treaty of alliance.",
